{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340712-has-anyone-played-a-swan-maiden","id":1340712,"title":"Has anyone played a Swan Maiden?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-10T20:17:40-07:00","id":1340712,"title":"Has anyone played a Swan Maiden?","content":"Or Swan Prince<br /> <br /> From the Changeling Players Guide<br /> <br /> I convinced my ST to change the Swan Maiden\u2019s weakness slightly so that they can have sex without penalty as long as they\u2019re truly in love with the person. I thought it was more romantic that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T08:30:36-07:00","id":1340780,"title":"","content":"Haven't played one, but I would def consider how you're viewing romance; it's not an objective idea. The Swan Maiden idea is a pretty toxic one, where a person's worth, their &quot;purity&quot; is tied to their sexuality, or lack thereof. It's built around the ethos that people should only have sex for the most practical reasons (children) and only when they have &quot;proven&quot; their love first (Marriage). Not going to tell you how you should/shouldn't play, but the idea is definitely meant to represent some pretty puritanical notions of sexuality, which are extremely rigid. According to their doctrine, sex isn't romantic, it is an occasionally necessary evil, in the most extreme of circumstances. In that ethos, to suffer is to be closer to god, and to feel pleasure is to succumb to temptation, showing weakness. Also note that the Frailty regarding intercourse doesn't actually HARM the Swan, it only stops her from accessing her birthright. She doesn't incur Banality or anything to that effect. It can still BE romantic, just not the 1700's puritanical notion of romance. The story they represent is a very anachronistic and frankly outdated one. The tension between representing a dying idea but being a living thing is sort of part and parcel to making Changelings what they are; in some form or another, they almost always represent an idea or story that is dying, and are trying to find a way to get by. Swan Maiden's specifically are walking tragedies (literally), guaranteed to either lose themselves or the ones they love, with the only recourse being to shut themselves away or break off their relationships (incurring banality, and thus being tragic anyway). Playing a Swan Maiden should not feel like a particularly comfortable or cushy experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","user":"RigelJ","date":". 10-11-2019, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T08:47:23-07:00","id":1340786,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25663\" data-vbnamecard=\"25663\">RigelJ</a> thank you!! You said exactly what I was thinking, except a lot more articulately. I'm gonna tell my ST that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T09:33:30-07:00","id":1340791,"title":"","content":"Haven't played one, but now I want to make a male of their bloodline, who ends up becoming a Swan Pooka as some kind of practical joke! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T10:35:42-07:00","id":1340801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340712-has-anyone-played-a-swan-maiden?p=1340791#post1340791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't played one, but now I want to make a male of their bloodline, who ends up becoming a Swan Pooka as some kind of practical joke! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lowkey, if I were a Swan Maiden, I would work my ass off to find a namer and become like any other kith SO fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T11:44:44-07:00","id":1340815,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I pretty much am anti-Swanmaid. I've seen it either depicted as the Taylor Swift &quot;short fling&quot; Kith, or the &quot;James Bond with a woman of the day,&quot; Kith. All while having a big ol-grabbag of bonuses, discount wings (I find discount merits lazy design), and just being thematically easier to replicate Oaths/Geases. Having &quot;You or them&quot; Dark Fate baked in cheapens any emotional pathos that could be had by playing them in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T20:07:43-07:00","id":1340892,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't see why Profound loss isn't the only Frailty... Most types only have one Frailty. If you wanted to give it more bite they could have to interact with people they love on a regular basis like any day they haven't at least talked to their loved ones counts as a Banality Trigger. Mantle of the Maiden is arbitrary. True Love's Curse is litterally pointless by the mechanics as.. you cannot buy Merits midgame, and even if you are allowing it... its super easy to get around...by never buying it.. plenty of people have commited loving relationships that don't count as &quot;True love' mechanically, just like plenty of people are deeply devoted to their faith without being able to turn vampires and perform miracles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T17:40:13-07:00","id":1341025,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. So you guys think playing a Swan Maiden is a terrible idea. I\u2019ll have to reread the rules more carefully and think about it. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25625_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25625\" data-vbnamecard=\"25625\">MagicJuggler</a> I actually like Taylor Swift, so that wouldn\u2019t discourage me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T17:59:56-07:00","id":1341030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340712-has-anyone-played-a-swan-maiden?p=1341025#post1341025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm. So you guys think playing a Swan Maiden is a terrible idea. I\u2019ll have to reread the rules more carefully and think about it. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the build is excessively Frailty heavy. If someone asked to play one I would not use anything but the first Frailty. I don't think &quot;Punish your character for having sex&quot; is a reasonable mechanic... and its one that is easily ignored (&quot;I'm only going ot fuck when not adventuring!&quot;) and hard to really impliment as an ST(&quot;Oh hey can you all tell me when your characters last fucked?&quot;)True Love's curse is even worse for pointlessness, it requires you take a merit to ever come up.<br /> <br /> I don't think dropping them would make the character profoundly unbalanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T04:06:01-07:00","id":1341073,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I\u2019ll talk to my ST about doing that if I decide to still play a Swan Maiden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T05:09:56-07:00","id":1341078,"title":"","content":"I talked to my ST. He said we could drop True Love\u2019s Curse and Mantle of the Maiden would only come into play if my character randomly hooks up with someone (as long as she has feelings for them, it doesn\u2019t count). I am gonna play a Swan Maiden. Thanks for all your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T19:41:19-07:00","id":1341378,"title":"","content":"Wait, I'm a little confused, because the Swan Maiden that you people are talking about is different from the information I've found on them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://changelingthedreaming.fandom.com/wiki/Swan_Maids\" target=\"_blank\">This specifically being the case.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T20:13:18-07:00","id":1341383,"title":"","content":"They are written up in the c20 players' guide.<br /> <br /> +1 app, +1 Dex can't botch performance. May buy wings for 2 points.<br /> <br /> Once per session may lower the difficulty of someone they are in love with.<br /> <br /> Frailties.<br /> <br /> Banality Trigger if they break up with someone.<br /> <br /> If they have sex they lose their second Birth right<br /> <br /> IF they have true love iwth someone either they or their true love recieve Dark Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T20:46:04-07:00","id":1341392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340712-has-anyone-played-a-swan-maiden?p=1340791#post1340791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't played one, but now I want to make a male of their bloodline, who ends up becoming a Swan Pooka as some kind of practical joke! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a clever idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T06:55:28-07:00","id":1341434,"title":"","content":"Just wanna say that there is a lot of negativity going on here. While I personally agree that the Swan Maiden kith could have been structured a little better, I actually think they offer more narrative than say a Selkie. Nothing on the Selkie Birthright/Frailty actually provides a plot hook beyond &quot;NPC stole my coat&quot;, and how many times can you actually run that story? Swan Maidens intrinsically offer tension and exist as a criticism of real issues that exist in our world, so like... yeah, they could be built a little better, but like also lets not jump down @Penelope's throat. We're all Changeling fans here, and that makes us all super weird. Swan Maidens might not be perfect, but lets face it, Changeling has had worse issues in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","user":"RigelJ","date":". 10-15-2019, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T04:38:01-07:00","id":1341613,"title":"","content":"I ended up creating an Unseelie Swan Maiden who defies the conventions of her kith and helps people understand that sex is a beautiful thing if you have feelings for the person. I picked this particular kith because I really am good at giving romantic advice and I wanted to play a character more like myself for a change. She has the Profound Loss Frailty and the Mantle of the Maiden Frailty, except that it doesn\u2019t come into play if she\u2019s in love with the person. (I really wanted her to be able to hook up without penalty during those periods when she\u2019s not actually in love with someone, but my ST absolutely refused to go for that). True Love\u2019s Curse was totally dropped.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25663\" data-vbnamecard=\"25663\">RigelJ</a> your analysis really helped. Hopefully this addresses some of the points you raised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T05:19:51-07:00","id":1341616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RigelJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340712-has-anyone-played-a-swan-maiden?p=1340801#post1340801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lowkey, if I were a Swan Maiden, I would work my ass off to find a namer and become like any other kith SO fast.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, I would, too. Not only is the kith forced to take a vow of celibacy for life, but any attempt to form a romantic attachment is doomed to end in tragedy for at least one of them?<br /> <br /> Swan Maidens sound like they sprang from the dreams of an anti-social masochist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T17:24:49-07:00","id":1341743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RigelJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340712-has-anyone-played-a-swan-maiden?p=1341434#post1341434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wanna say that there is a lot of negativity going on here. While I personally agree that the Swan Maiden kith could have been structured a little better, I actually think they offer more narrative than say a Selkie. Nothing on the Selkie Birthright/Frailty actually provides a plot hook beyond &quot;NPC stole my coat&quot;, and how many times can you actually run that story? Swan Maidens intrinsically offer tension and exist as a criticism of real issues that exist in our world, so like... yeah, they could be built a little better, but like also lets not jump down @Penelope's throat. We're all Changeling fans here, and that makes us all super weird. Swan Maidens might not be perfect, but lets face it, Changeling has had worse issues in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not jumping down Penelope's throat. I think the mechanics of it are questionable and don't even have &quot;But myth&quot; as a basis.. I mean in myth Swan maids are just basically Selkie variants in at least the folklore I've seen. I mean its.. kind fo weird Swanmaids.. don't turn into swans.<br /> <br /> On the other hand there's plenty of room for Angels of love as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}